# Root-level ignore, shared by every Vercel project connected to this repo
# (perigee-core AND web) - Vercel strips these paths from the checkout before
# ANY project's Root Directory is applied, so this file must never exclude a
# directory another project's build actually needs. web/ was excluded here
# once; that broke web's own "Root Directory: web" build with "No Next.js
# version detected" the moment its Git integration was connected, because
# there was nothing left under web/ to find a package.json in.
#
# Only truly universal junk belongs here: multi-gigabyte trees nothing
# builds from directly (mobile/'s node_modules alone is ~1GB, which is what
# this file exists to keep out of a `vercel deploy` run from the repo root).
mobile/
node_modules/
backend/node_modules/
backend/.venv/
backend/__pycache__/
backend/.pytest_cache/
backend/.ruff_cache/
backend/tests/
backend/fixtures/
web/node_modules/
web/.next/
.git/

# CRITICAL: Vercel prefers pyproject.toml over requirements.txt when present,
# and backend/pyproject.toml declares NO runtime dependencies (it is only
# ruff/pytest/pyright config). Shipping it makes the build install nothing and
# every request fail with FUNCTION_INVOCATION_FAILED. backend/.vercelignore
# excludes it for the same reason; this file must too.
backend/pyproject.toml
